{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PHP",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " therefore any consolation in Christ, if any comfort of love, if any fellowship of the Spirit, if any bowels and mercies,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fulfill ye my joy, that ye be like-minded, having the same love, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of one accord, of one mind.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " nothing ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be done",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " through strife or vain glory; but in lowliness of mind let each esteem other better than themselves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Look not every man on his own things, but every man also on the things of others.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let this mind be in you, which was also in Christ Jesus:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who, being in the form of God, thought it not robbery to be equal with God:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But made himself of no reputation, and took upon him the form of a servant, and was made in the likeness of men:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And being found in fashion as a man, he humbled himself, and became obedient to death, even the death of the cross.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore God also hath highly exalted him, and given him a name which is above every name:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in heaven, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on earth, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " under the earth;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Lord, to the glory of God the Father.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore, my beloved, as ye have always obeyed, not as in my presence only, but now much more in my absence, work out your own salvation with fear and trembling.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it is God who worketh in you both to will and to do of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good pleasure.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do all things without murmurings and disputings:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That ye may be blameless and harmless, the sons of God, without rebuke, in the midst of a crooked and perverse nation, among whom ye shine as lights in the world;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Holding forth the word of life; that I may rejoice in the day of Christ, that I have not run in vain, neither labored in vain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if I am even offered upon the sacrifice and service of your faith, I joy, and rejoice with you all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the same cause also do ye joy, and rejoice with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I trust in the Lord Jesus to send Timothy shortly to you, that I also may be of good comfort, when I know your state.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I have no man like-minded, who will naturally care for your state.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For all seek their own, not the things of Jesus Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But ye know the proof of him, that as a son with the father, he hath served with me in the gospel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Him therefore I hope to send presently, so soon as I shall see how it will go with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I trust in the Lord that I also myself shall come shortly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet I supposed it necessary to send to you Epaphroditus, my brother, and companion in labor, and fellow-soldier, but your messenger, and he that ministered to my wants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he longed after you all, and was full of heaviness, because ye had heard that he was sick.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For indeed he was sick nigh to death: but God had mercy on him; and not on him only, but on me also, lest I should have sorrow upon sorrow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I sent him therefore the more speedily, that, when ye see him again, ye may rejoice, and that I may be the less sorrowful.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Receive him therefore in the Lord with all gladness; and hold such in reputation:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.2.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.2.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because for the work of Christ he was nigh to death, not regarding his life, to supply the want of your service towards me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
